# Supabase migrations

Migrations are append-only, like git commits.

- Never edit an already-applied or merged migration. To change schema, write a **new** migration file.
- One logical change per file — do not cram unrelated table changes into one migration (harder to review and roll back).
- Every migration that adds a table must enable RLS in that same file. No table may exist, even briefly, without RLS.
- `supabase/seed.sql` is local/dev only. Never apply seeds automatically to staging or production.
- Any PR that touches `supabase/migrations/` must review the SQL itself, not only app code. Schema changes are often higher-risk than application changes.
- Whenever you add or change a migration, **always update** `Docs/schema.dbml` (tables, enums, indexes, FKs, RLS notes) and `Docs/supabase-functions.md` (functions, RPCs, procedures, triggers — name, role, details, how it works) so both stay in sync with applied SQL.
